40,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, that was eye-opening! It turns out our depots never stop during peak season, and those 2021 tools were basically replaced by spreadsheets almost immediately. We really need a vendor who can handle that chaos!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings suggest a concerning pattern. While initial capital costs are scrutinized, recurring operating expenses often slip through. Furthermore, separate add-ons have seen yearly price hikes, unlike bundled agreements. We must be wary of hidden long-term costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are equally concerning. Last winter's outage remained unowned for two days due to fragmented support contracts, and our warehouse rules were rewritten twice within a year, rendering the initial project scope obsolete.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found some scary stuff! The dispatch tool is super old and they skipped updates because they were too busy. Plus, some outside people messed up the 2018 pay move and it took a whole year to fix!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems we are all discovering that the cracks in our foundation are deeper than we imagined. My research reveals a fragile human bridge; we are losing vital knowledge and struggling to replace it.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki @Asuka @Rin @Servas, it sounds like we're all seeing a pattern of things breaking or being ignored. If our yard tools are just spreadsheets and the support is fragmented, we can't afford another failure!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Asuka"",""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Exactly. We cannot simply look at the initial quote. If we choose a vendor with fragmented licensing or hidden add-ons, we will face the same uncontrolled cost creep I discovered in the renewal invoices.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji @Mizuki, the issue isn't just the tools, but the lack of accountability. If we don't secure a single point of ownership and a flexible scope, we will repeat the same failures regardless of the vendor.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! We can't just let things get old and dusty like that dispatch tool, and we definitely can't let outsiders leave us with a big mess to clean up for a whole year!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Indeed. We must remember that a system is only as strong as the hands that guide it. If our experts depart and our supervisors resist, even the finest software will become a burden.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I totally agree! We need a partner who doesn't just sell us software, but actually helps our people use it. If the system is too hard for the depot staff, they'll just go back to spreadsheets!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"That is a valid point, Kenji. However, we must ensure that ""help"" doesn't come as a series of expensive, separate service contracts. I will be looking for a vendor that offers a comprehensive, bundled pricing model.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, bundling costs is a start, but it doesn't solve the ownership problem. We need a vendor who accepts full accountability for system stability and allows for agile scope adjustments as our business needs evolve.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Asuka! We need someone who stays and helps us fix things, not someone who just does a ""data lift"" and disappears while we spend a year cleaning up their mess!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must seek a partner who values the human spirit. A vendor who provides deep, patient training and supports our remaining staff will prevent our wisdom from vanishing as our veterans retire.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"It sounds like we're all on the same page! We need a vendor who is tough enough for the yard, clear on costs, accountable for fixes, and patient with our people. I'm ready to see the candidates!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. We have identified the critical risks: hidden costs, fragmented support, technical debt, and knowledge loss. I will evaluate the candidates based on their ability to provide a transparent, all-inclusive financial model.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will prioritize a vendor that guarantees a single point of contact for support and demonstrates a flexible approach to scope management. We cannot afford another project that becomes obsolete before it is even fully deployed.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'll be looking for someone who keeps things fresh and doesn't leave us with a giant puzzle to solve alone! No more skipping updates or messy hand-offs for me! I'm ready!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Servas,,"The path forward is clear. We must choose a partner who sees our employees not as users, but as the heart of the operation. I shall vote for the one who offers the most grace.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
