65,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at these, Anchor Industrial Software seems like the best bet! They have an engineering team present through rollout, which is exactly what we need to make sure it survives the yard and our peak season.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I must disagree with Anchor. On-premise servers often lead to hidden maintenance costs. Corvus is even worse; its modular, independent licensing is exactly the kind of fragmented pricing that leads to the cost creep I discovered.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki I agree that Corvus is a risk. Its modular, independent licensing likely mirrors the fragmented support that caused our last outage. We need a unified system, not a collection of separate components.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I don't like Anchor either! They put it on our own servers, and that's how the dispatch tool got old and dusty. We need something that stays updated automatically so we don't skip things again!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Servas,,"My heart leans toward Anchor as well. Having their engineers present during the rollout provides the steady hand our stretched staff needs, ensuring the knowledge is transferred and the people are truly supported.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I get that, but having the engineers right here means they can see the chaos in the yard for themselves! They can't just ignore us if they're standing right there.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, physical presence doesn't guarantee financial transparency. Meridian Systems offers a hosted suite with a fixed configuration, which is far more likely to provide the predictable, bundled cost structure we need to avoid future budget surprises.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, a fixed configuration is a trap. My research showed that our business needs change mid-year. A rigid process will lead to the same obsolete scope we suffered before. We need the flexibility of Tessera.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I like Tessera's flexibility, but wait! They use a ""partner firm"" for the migration and training. That sounds like those outside people who messed up the pay move and left us to clean it up!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your caution is wise. A third party can indeed be a bridge to nowhere. However, we must weigh that risk against the exhaustion of our own people. A fixed system may break their spirit.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka @Mizuki, if Meridian is too rigid and Tessera uses outside partners, Anchor is still the strongest! Their engineers are actually here, which means they can't just leave us with a mess or a system that doesn't work.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, physical presence is a temporary comfort. Once the rollout ends, we are left with the long-term burden of server maintenance and unpredictable costs. Meridian's hosted suite is the only option that ensures financial predictability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, predictability is useless if the system is obsolete. @Kenji, Anchor's presence is temporary. Tessera's configurable workflows are the only way to prevent the scope from failing again, provided we hold the vendor accountable for their partner.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I'm still worried about that partner firm! But Meridian sounds too stiff and Anchor is just more dusty servers. Maybe Tessera is okay if we make them promise to stay and help?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, your intuition is a guiding light. While Tessera offers flexibility, the risk of a detached partner is great. Anchor's presence offers the most compassion for our weary souls during the transition.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm sticking with Anchor! We can't risk another ""spreadsheet solution"" because the software was too rigid or the partners disappeared. Having their engineers on-site is the only way to ensure it actually works in our yards. I vote Anchor!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I cannot support Anchor or Corvus due to the high risk of hidden costs and fragmented pricing. While Tessera is flexible, Meridian's hosted suite provides the most transparent and predictable financial model. I vote Meridian Systems!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, predictability is a facade if the system cannot adapt. @Kenji, on-site engineers are a temporary fix for a structural problem. Tessera's configurable workflows are the only way to avoid obsolescence. I vote Tessera Cloud Suite!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm still scared of the partner firm, but I'm even more scared of dusty servers and stiff systems! Tessera seems like the best way to keep things fresh and flexible. I vote Tessera Cloud Suite!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Servas,,"The weight of our people's exhaustion cannot be ignored. While others seek flexibility or predictability, I seek stability for the human heart. Anchor's commitment to be present is the kindness we need. I vote Anchor Industrial Software.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
